<http://www.spektrix.com/theporttheatre/event/99601AGQDKBRDSRMRNNGRRPPTNKPBKTMQ> a
    schema:Event;
  schema:name "Luminous Music of the Soul";
  schema:description """
	What happens when a fantastic pianist, a fabulous string quartet and an amazing choir get together? They shine a light on how deeply, evocative music can strike at our heartstrings.  Ola Gjeilo’s “Luminous Music of the Night” is a feature work for the Island Consort’s fall program.  The string quartet are players from the Nanaimo Chamber Orchestra and the pianist is young musical phenom, Liam Pistor – who will also feature as guest soloist to play works by Chopin and Brahms.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“Luminous Music of the Soul” is a program that breathes life into classical choral repertoire for the audience to enjoy.  Beginning with an English madrigal, it comprises an adaptation of Beethoven’s Moonlight Sonata, “Benedictus” – from a mass by Canadian, Tim Corlis, a re-imagination of Panis Angelicus, and works by Randall Thompson, Anton Bruckner, Gabriel Faure and Michael Snelgrove. The program ends with three ‘seasonal’ songs, as a nod to Christmas; Gloucester Wassail, Deck the Halls, and the premiere of “When Shiloh Came”; a lovely piece written by Island Consort’s Randall Donald.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-28T14:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/theporttheatre/files/8ffef451-6b5f-4615-b8b1-80ba4187ad68.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/theporttheatre/location/412AHMGMKLQDMMDQBVNMGMNLDCBBPTLQP>;
  schema:organizer <https://spektrix.com/theporttheatre/organization/island-consort-chamber-choir>;
  schema:offers _:9ec39dc5c604456196f82735f7e99ad45196;
  schema:keywords "Offsite Events";
  schema:duration "PT120M";
  schema:endDate "2026-11-28T16:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

